#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171830 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "91f986c6-c305-50eb-a5b7-36043279d128" :question/math-academy-id "e-9505" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/3a24d08f3fce05b0a69b361d96cde0766860e0fd466a2622d780572334b2deba.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/d910373a10dd1d08aed3df8b6b40102f4f1cc42e94e099ba6c74e6c5065828a1.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/05831230ea1993c0df5f2dae6d6411da094f181006980ea261a5b55fc9f21b40.png)" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171831 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9779a982-2048-58e2-8a90-df2bcb366d96" :question/math-academy-id "e-9506" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/f017ccc60a7c1bb9ac09978492c9db217836099d0926ee009ffc44ba827c25d5.png)" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/514520062cf4564f58267774ba6b50027f9cd27dedfa392cb7038f94580b1e4a.png)\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171832 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2ddc4e15-3729-5425-953c-1cb95edc201b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9508" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/43bcde1806155410ba97b0b2e5807d4a0f9cee93ef04f2ccfb413552de74178b.png)" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb5255d2-d627-567c-8c35-bac5df06fc84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168566} {:answer/id #uuid "34dbd31b-8938-56f2-9424-45480b06918a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168567} {:answer/id #uuid "51622226-72a9-5301-a849-342ad3393fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168568} {:answer/id #uuid "54742cc8-1d74-54ad-aaec-d89be577e875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168569} {:answer/id #uuid "5f25c3d3-e3a0-584e-8db8-aa554c35846c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51622226-72a9-5301-a849-342ad3393fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168568} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd62ae1-252a-5373-b2b8-205eb305fd0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01d5649d-0bb8-52a3-be74-234b60c39fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-124091" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-u+av+b,\\,y=2u-5v+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 2u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v+2 \\\\ 2u-5v+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-u+4v+2,\\,y=2u-5v+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+2+1=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4db05b93-9101-50eb-867f-1be169ca5a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374781} {:answer/id #uuid "d2df3a64-9ca4-58c0-a5ed-0c2937f9db1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374782} {:answer/id #uuid "fe087dab-d7e2-51eb-8c62-c8c248f99d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374783} {:answer/id #uuid "cc53c711-b6f8-5e08-82ae-a08659a9938b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374784} {:answer/id #uuid "862fa672-7f20-554d-838d-2f95b5dac9c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc53c711-b6f8-5e08-82ae-a08659a9938b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374784} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd2eb17b-7d2b-5a7d-84d3-216b6cdf99dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac6412d1-cb10-5766-a34f-06f77acc0dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-124237" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec601d4b-260d-51a4-bffb-9b036f6ce175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374788} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0195a8-8b8f-5dd8-b0ba-32e72c30a66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374789} {:answer/id #uuid "afab2577-2fdd-5684-8439-2067490765a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374790} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4b4651-3ec4-5e10-998c-2bbc7e44fc1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374791} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5035b0-eb00-5d8f-a8e3-4ded7963bc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afab2577-2fdd-5684-8439-2067490765a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374790} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52cfc52-d529-5c0f-b98a-4493dc35cb41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbb420fe-a3d6-5837-9a10-bc99b9694665" :question/math-academy-id "q-124245" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7u-v+6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7u-v \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8v-9u \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9u+8v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-5 \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 8u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1eb52d-5918-531a-847e-e7183292a357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295113} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} {:answer/id #uuid "4921b728-e559-5950-b1e1-5d48b087121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295115} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc8898e-b8a2-5834-92d5-7b2cacef4d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295116} {:answer/id #uuid "62384ace-b84c-5e85-95f4-b664393de08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} :answer-field/id #uuid "9adf5d47-b90f-57ec-9563-b1300c861940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7c49d1f-62c6-5240-9ecd-d0ff7b646237" :question/math-academy-id "q-124247" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} {:answer/id #uuid "ac90f967-da15-5704-9665-c9929cd922e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295128} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f73f23-5f24-5207-95b5-1a3853e0f1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295129} {:answer/id #uuid "4456ce1b-97eb-545d-b767-dd68122091aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295130} {:answer/id #uuid "750596c5-9b6f-5472-a950-f0c1ea73740f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} :answer-field/id #uuid "482bb424-6613-54b7-891f-74ee4de3f263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "111538d1-a3c4-5a8b-bb3b-b571c7d190d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124253" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60222e43-7ac3-5ed4-9eda-bc50a2a55c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374794} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b03463-4875-51d7-bfa3-4891a7c3726d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374795} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad5264d-280c-5a88-ae0f-a2245652f985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374796} {:answer/id #uuid "6f23e5f8-fb98-5331-bf8f-63ebd93c2a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374797} {:answer/id #uuid "f92dd7d3-2b81-5f6f-8d07-1ae2a7dec327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f92dd7d3-2b81-5f6f-8d07-1ae2a7dec327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374798} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee2a9412-d172-50e9-9ba7-0380d53df00d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5cb4053-f0cc-5e78-b06a-329e6bd661d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124255" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv+1 \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u+v \\\\ -u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{3}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "761e281b-e631-5212-a160-f8db9cbeaac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295134} {:answer/id #uuid "38946076-2c0f-5674-80f6-7effeb0eb079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295135} {:answer/id #uuid "269d906d-77b3-5906-989e-e1566c26e416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295136} {:answer/id #uuid "822087bb-8c5c-53ed-ba35-dc591995de18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295137} {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cbccf9-50b4-50d4-af0b-6b7102c9915e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fbd649a-72ec-5c96-b929-3b7a8cd0013b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124259" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be48af4-b946-5e8b-ab28-4f792a31a974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295141} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9d9ce5-d759-57bf-80a9-b7ceff4906fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295142} {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} {:answer/id #uuid "2180f3a8-6e9c-5b8a-af2d-60e6a57d55c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295144} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9683bb-89bc-5459-b095-601993cf9cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} :answer-field/id #uuid "0df96ffa-72ad-5985-a938-cb8d42f45297" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42e18668-b4ac-5ec0-a619-27855b78e8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124261" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv-2,\\,y=u+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v \\\\ u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v-2 \\\\ u+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=6u+8v-2,\\,y=u+5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+8+5=19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374799 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4890714-068b-5bf8-a44d-03713cbdc955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374801} {:answer/id #uuid "0227216a-608f-5be2-8741-8bc7848db3ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374802} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7a1dad-dc96-5891-bf7f-73438908dc3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374803} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3ede1d-57fd-5385-94e0-fd7676b38d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374804} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed61de2-2e2e-537a-817e-1e7637f22921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a3ede1d-57fd-5385-94e0-fd7676b38d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374804} :answer-field/id #uuid "3723268d-c0c3-5c50-aca2-c113bfa41873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "15af8fa0-939a-538f-bf0d-f7bc0f9be4f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124265" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+6v+b,\\,y=cu-4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+6v \\\\ 3u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+6v \\\\ 3u-4v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+6v+0,\\,y=3u-4v\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+3=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0454c184-1c2d-5a83-bc6b-26f4ddd9868d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374808} {:answer/id #uuid "40bb26e3-044e-53b1-86bf-5d14daaa400e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374809} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e23783-c493-5579-991e-3f3f3dbe156b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374810} {:answer/id #uuid "bea08ebe-8684-5d87-a6ea-53edf0d9f986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374811} {:answer/id #uuid "9cbfa0f9-ea53-52ff-8d1c-2c391d28931c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9e23783-c493-5579-991e-3f3f3dbe156b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374810} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d7c6a6a-2241-50d0-a7f3-98f81c19de70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b034ca82-3f60-54db-9d6f-5f61b609df29" :question/math-academy-id "q-124267" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au-2v+b,\\,y=4u+cv-2\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u-2v \\\\ 4u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u-2v+1 \\\\ 4u+7v-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-6u-2v+1,\\,y=4u+7v-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+1+7=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b35623-d326-5fb9-91ba-e8f93b1fe7db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295163} {:answer/id #uuid "ec74b222-bfdc-5fd9-9901-d062abb31c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295164} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8d000c-d154-5174-9dc0-69d3a40286ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295165} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9ac776-4ed0-511c-a57a-d8c2c9d6502c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} :answer-field/id #uuid "879f4cc5-b9a7-5a26-b6f3-bc229be46c40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94ef537c-d453-5e44-8027-fc902bea1259" :question/math-academy-id "q-124284" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} {:answer/id #uuid "8e14f16e-9b4e-58f1-906b-1eee902250fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295170} {:answer/id #uuid "38e23b92-2a75-5dfc-bdf4-513200c83294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295171} {:answer/id #uuid "1edbfb1c-9a04-5adb-89fb-bf120ffd3ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295172} {:answer/id #uuid "f61e3520-7d0e-5c7c-96cf-a5c357e7b01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} :answer-field/id #uuid "313376e7-eb16-55f0-8f6e-6a40eb0fdbb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb3e7867-83ca-5695-bc9b-8585b1f7a576" :question/math-academy-id "q-124285" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u-3v-2,\\,y=2u+v+7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-2)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "809f9a0a-4f00-5123-a4ce-549ee540a4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168584} {:answer/id #uuid "b3022db4-1f80-5fac-8c95-8dc867e2a56e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168585} {:answer/id #uuid "c681f1e8-a89e-5685-805e-db71df9a74b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168586} {:answer/id #uuid "cf62493d-963c-53a0-9fd8-28a7b527027b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168587} {:answer/id #uuid "e2814013-c948-5ca7-9400-e16d674a34b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "809f9a0a-4f00-5123-a4ce-549ee540a4c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168584} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab467d1e-fc91-59e3-98c2-999b1925200f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8d697d1-ccf8-518a-9776-12fda551dcda" :question/math-academy-id "q-124291" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u+3,\\,y=7v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u \\\\ -u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=5+(-1)+3=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d4f990-96c3-50b1-b1ac-4c662c0d4982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374815} {:answer/id #uuid "083f7c31-579c-5f76-84c9-e9639aabc0f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374816} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc8208b-8ca1-5323-94d6-a802c6ee8697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374817} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc3bc15-3cea-5e4d-a036-ba92d344dc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374818} {:answer/id #uuid "47634270-6b42-509e-89bf-8a463eb83d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dc3bc15-3cea-5e4d-a036-ba92d344dc8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374818} :answer-field/id #uuid "d77a5f81-8a0b-52fd-a1d4-fd84664c96cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "302233c5-435a-5344-a779-daf789f391bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124295" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-5v-2,\\,y=7v-2u-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ -2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v \\\\ -2u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-5+7+(-2)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5492cc5-8266-527b-b2cf-8d5f5fdc432f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295183} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe44c9c-07b3-55d3-820f-f382ef124b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295184} {:answer/id #uuid "521bba8c-2428-52ba-852a-ac6683eb7c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295185} {:answer/id #uuid "0441e29b-bd6e-54e6-9755-0a4053ddb78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295186} {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a507a4-26f1-59b0-af28-c13d74c534ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27624eaf-a41b-5122-b27f-be42134ea00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124301" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u-v,\\,y=2u-3v+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 \\\\ 2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+(-3)+4=7.\n$$"}]}
